WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:04.437 --> 00:00:05.972
So were you kind
of adventurous

00:00:06.039 --> 00:00:07.640
when you are growing up, or--

00:00:07.707 --> 00:00:10.343
I wanted to be Indiana Jones
when I was younger, but then--

00:00:10.410 --> 00:00:11.044
Really?

00:00:11.111 --> 00:00:12.345
--I also was super shy.

00:00:12.412 --> 00:00:14.180
And were you like, sporty?

00:00:14.247 --> 00:00:15.849
No, not at all.

00:00:15.915 --> 00:00:17.117
BEAR GRYLLS: So
what, more geeky?

00:00:17.183 --> 00:00:18.284
I was super geeky.

00:00:18.351 --> 00:00:19.753
BEAR GRYLLS: [laughs]

00:00:19.819 --> 00:00:22.155
This is basically my
audition for Indiana Jones.

00:00:22.222 --> 00:00:24.891
[laughs] OK.

00:00:24.958 --> 00:00:26.393
Let's get into this.

00:00:26.459 --> 00:00:28.328
Now this is mangrove swamp.

00:00:28.395 --> 00:00:30.029
This is the start of it.

00:00:30.096 --> 00:00:31.765
It's actually a pretty
amazing ecosystem,

00:00:31.831 --> 00:00:35.702
because it's just so full of
incredible, diverse wildlife.

00:00:35.769 --> 00:00:39.139
Lot of crocs, by the way, you
know, further into this stuff.

00:00:39.205 --> 00:00:41.241
But this is the start
of the mangrove,

00:00:41.307 --> 00:00:44.411
and we need to be
going this way.

00:00:44.477 --> 00:00:46.212
It's going to be fun, right?

00:00:46.279 --> 00:00:47.447
What's the worst
that could happen?

00:00:47.514 --> 00:00:49.382
Yeah, This is going
to be many things.

00:00:49.449 --> 00:00:51.017
Fun is not going
to be one of them.

00:00:51.084 --> 00:00:51.851
OK.

00:00:51.918 --> 00:00:52.986
Let's do it.

00:00:53.052 --> 00:00:56.823
[music playing]

00:01:01.127 --> 00:01:03.029
Whoa-ho-ho.

00:01:03.096 --> 00:01:05.298
This, as a survivalist, is good.

00:01:05.365 --> 00:01:08.401
God, look at the
size of that one.

00:01:08.468 --> 00:01:09.035
Oh, look--

00:01:09.102 --> 00:01:10.203
[gasps]

00:01:10.270 --> 00:01:13.473
That's a rhino
beetle grub, larvae.

00:01:13.540 --> 00:01:14.874
Look at that.

00:01:14.941 --> 00:01:15.775
There's another one.

00:01:15.842 --> 00:01:17.076
You get that one out.

00:01:17.143 --> 00:01:18.611
Oh, my gosh.

00:01:18.678 --> 00:01:21.714
Good protein,
good snack, this is.

00:01:21.781 --> 00:01:23.249
BEAR GRYLLS (VOICEOVER):
As a general rule,

00:01:23.316 --> 00:01:25.218
raw grubs are edible.

00:01:25.285 --> 00:01:27.787
They have more protein,
pound for pound, than beef.

00:01:27.854 --> 00:01:31.658
And they are plentiful in dark,
damp places all over the world.

00:01:31.724 --> 00:01:33.793
But it's critical
that they're purged

00:01:33.860 --> 00:01:36.229
before consumption,
in case they've eaten

00:01:36.296 --> 00:01:38.298
something poisonous to humans.

00:01:38.364 --> 00:01:40.533
BEAR GRYLLS: So
look, grab the head.

00:01:40.600 --> 00:01:41.668
No.

00:01:41.734 --> 00:01:43.203
And then you just
twist the head, pull

00:01:43.269 --> 00:01:48.041
that off, and then all of that.

00:01:48.107 --> 00:01:50.877
[laughs] Your face, I love it.

00:01:50.944 --> 00:01:53.413
What just fell out of it?

00:01:53.480 --> 00:01:55.148
I think some
really medieval guts.

00:01:55.215 --> 00:01:57.817
You squeezed his heart out.

00:01:57.884 --> 00:02:01.120
Listen, that's many things,
but that's not a heart.

00:02:01.187 --> 00:02:03.490
I think that's his anal tract.

00:02:03.556 --> 00:02:04.791
[laughing] Ew.

00:02:04.858 --> 00:02:08.061
BEAR GRYLLS: [laughs] And
then you're left with that,

00:02:08.127 --> 00:02:10.063
and that's all good.

00:02:10.129 --> 00:02:10.897
Good energy.

00:02:10.964 --> 00:02:12.432
Little skin.

00:02:12.499 --> 00:02:13.566
Do you want me to go first,
or do you want to go first?

00:02:13.633 --> 00:02:14.767
- I'll do it with you.
- Oh, OK.

00:02:14.834 --> 00:02:16.069
Here we go.

00:02:16.135 --> 00:02:17.437
I don't think I got
all the anal tract out,

00:02:17.504 --> 00:02:19.205
but what's the worst
that could happen, right?

00:02:19.272 --> 00:02:20.106
Just adds the flavor.

00:02:20.173 --> 00:02:21.107
OK, great.

00:02:25.945 --> 00:02:29.048
I just a beetle larva.

00:02:29.115 --> 00:02:32.585
I'd rather not explain
what it tastes like.

00:02:32.652 --> 00:02:33.286
Ugh.

00:02:33.353 --> 00:02:34.320
Doesn't taste very good.

00:02:34.387 --> 00:02:34.988
No.

00:02:35.054 --> 00:02:36.055
But good energy.

00:02:36.122 --> 00:02:37.357
Feel energized, I guess.

00:02:37.423 --> 00:02:38.658
Yeah.

00:02:38.725 --> 00:02:40.527
I think I'm supposed to feel
more energized than I do.

00:02:40.593 --> 00:02:41.594
I think the cappuccinos
work better.

